{"scenario":"dts-arq-short-family-window-128","rows":["C-0052","C-0063","C-0168","C-0170","C-0190","C-0558","C-0730","C-0762","C-0766","C-0769","C-0770","C-0771","C-0772","C-0773","C-0774","C-0775","C-0780","C-0781","C-0782","C-0185","C-0186","C-1122","C-0850","C-1127","C-0367","C-0886","C-1154","C-1191","C-1193","B-0125","B-0140","B-0141","B-0232","B-0408","B-0409","A-0194","A-0321","C-0426","C-1260"],"source":"Ed4 C.7.2 (g) to (j), p.C-99; C.4.3, p.C-22; B.7.2.2, p.B-31","description":"On a link between Ed4 peers negotiated Short the 8-bit family is used, and at most 128 D_PDUs are outstanding whatever dts.max_window says; once they are acknowledged FSNs continue from 128.","config":{"local_address":"0.0.1.2","csma":{"mode":"jitter"},"modem":{"preamble_ms":600,"flush_ms":150,"waveforms":[{"wn":2,"interleaver":"long","block_bytes":250,"block_ms":500}]},"cas":{"max_links":4,"link_request_timeout_ms":60000,"link_request_retries":2,"first_data_timeout_ms":120000},"dts":{"max_segment_size":7,"ack_wait_ms":60000}},"note":"Conn 1 binds SAP 9 for ARQ. At 2000 the peer 0.0.1.3 calls with Short and Ed4 set (octet 16); we accept with Short and Ed4 (octet 26, B-0140, B-0409), so the link uses the Ed3 D_PDUs between Ed4 peers by agreement (C-0052, C-0063, C-0168, B-0141, B-0232) and the peer is recorded Ed4 (B-0408). The accept goes out at 52000 (EOT and reception window 2), and since the peer is recorded Ed4 its block is filled with 20 PADDING D_PDUs (C-0367, C-1154). The link is made when it ends at 53250: window edges TX LWE 0, TX UWE 255 (C-0782). At 61500 the client sends a 904-byte U_PDU to SAP 5 (TTL 0), so the DATA C_PDU is 910 bytes (the same 6-byte header as in dts-arq/data-ack-merge, made at the same time), cut at dts.max_segment_size 7 into 130 segments. dts.ttd starts; the channel has been idle since our own transmission, so LBT_WAIT with lbt_wait_vdcd_ms 3000 (K-0066, K-0074), then contention 12000 ms (second draw). At 76500 the transmission could hold 253 blocks, but dts.max_window 32768 is more than the 8-bit family allows, so the maximum allowable window is 128 (C-0771, C-0773, C-1193): ED3-DATA-ONLY (type 0) FSNs 0 to 127 go, each with DELIVER IN ORDER, C_PDU START on FSN 0 only, no C_PDU END, TX WIN LWE on FSN 0 and TX WIN UWE on FSN 127 (C-0185, C-0186, C-1122), and the window is then full, so the other two segments wait (C-0774, C-0775, C-1127). Each D_PDU is 25 bytes, so ten fill each 250-byte block and none crosses a boundary: block alignment towards this Ed4 peer changes nothing (C-1191). 3200 bytes need 13 blocks; the 50 spare bytes of the last take 4 PADDING D_PDUs, as the peer is Ed4 (C-0367, C-1191). EOT 14 - b in block b. dts.ack_wait/0.0.1.3 starts when the transmission ends at 83750. At 91000 the peer's ED3-ACK-ONLY with RX LWE 128 and no SELECTIVE ACKS acknowledges FSNs 0 to 127 and TX LWE moves to 128 (C-0780, C-0781): dts.ack_wait stops; the C_PDU is not yet confirmed. The burst ends at 92000: csma.vdcd_end to 96000, LBT rule 1, contention 45000 ms (third draw). At 141000 the last two segments go with FSNs 128 and 129, modulo 256 (C-0190, C-0766): TX WIN LWE on 128, TX WIN UWE and C_PDU END on 129; one block, EOT 2, its 200 spare bytes taking 18 PADDING D_PDUs. dts.ack_wait starts at 142250. Fixture: preamble 600, flush 150, 250 bytes and 500 ms a block, so an n-block transmission lasts 750 + 500 n ms and the EOT of a D_PDU starting in block b of n is ceil((500 (n - b) + 150) / 500) = n - b + 1 (C-0104, C-1043). Addresses 0.0.1.2 and 0.0.1.3 take address size 3 (C-0133): a type 0 is 18 bytes plus its segment, a PADDING D_PDU 11 bytes, a type 8 carrying a one-byte CAS-1 C_PDU 25 bytes. The U_PDU's byte i is i mod 251. Seed 0 draws uniform(16) = 15, 4, 15: contention waits 45000, 12000, 45000 ms (K-0080).  The SIS soft link times are unset, so they are derived: sis.soft_link_idle and sis.soft_link_min_hold (called node only) three answer waits, sis.soft_link_max six; none falls due within the run, and the idle wait stops while an ARQ U_PDU is outstanding (A-0320, A-0321, A-0326). Since corpus 0.28.0 (P7-3), every D_PDU this node sends to a peer recorded Ed4 carries EOW 0xF01, CAPABILITY (Ed4 1, Duplex 0), where it carried EMPTY (C-0426, C-1260); an owed UNRECOGNIZED-TYPE-ERROR still goes first (C-1079), and D_PDUs to a peer of unknown edition, a peer recorded Ed3 or a group carry EMPTY as before. Where this note says EOW 0 or EMPTY for such a D_PDU, read CAPABILITY. Only EOW and header CRC bytes changed."}
